# Server variant of omarchy-iso/builder/archinstall.packages: the package set
# pacstrap installs into the target before the Omarchy runtime, and the seed of
# the ISO's offline mirror.
#
# Differences from the desktop list:
#   - dropped: pipewire, alsa-firmware, sof-firmware (a server has no audio
#     stack).
#   - dropped: base-devel. A server carries no compiler and no build toolchain;
#     the ISO's early bootstrap no longer asks for it either (see the
#     orchestrator patch). `omarchy-server-addon dev` brings it back for the
#     machines that need to build something.
#   - dropped: tailscale. Optional software does not belong in the base; it is
#     bundled in the offline mirror through the `tailscale` addon instead.
#   - added: nano (`base` ships no editor and omarchy-nvim is not part of the
#     server profile).
#
# Note this file only seeds the offline mirror: archinstall decides on its own
# what pacstrap installs, so the packages that must really land in the target
# are in omarchy-server.packages, which the orchestrator reads back.
#
# Both microcode packages stay: the mirror must be able to serve either CPU.
amd-ucode
base
efibootmgr
intel-ucode
limine
linux
linux-firmware
nano
omarchy-keyring
openssh
snapper
